 PM · 75 minutes · Asia/Kolkata (IST)\n\nTIME BUDGET\n5 min — Recall th
 e method\n30 min — Lesson / worked example\n30 min — Independent attem
 pts\n10 min — Check and note the error\n\nWORK ORDER\nOpen the NCERT sec
 tion named in step 1. Use a matching video explanation OR the worked examp
 le within the learning budget\; do not try to finish both. Attempt the ste
 p 2 questions in the listed order with solutions covered. Reserve the chec
 king minutes. At the practice cutoff\, flag any unattempted or unresolved 
 question by number\; it goes to the buffer or next same-subject slot.\n\n1
 . LEARN / RECALL\nRead NCERT 5.2\, PDF pp. 1–13. Test continuity using L
 HL = RHL = f(a)\; simplify a removable discontinuity before substituting.\
 n\n2. INDEPENDENT PRACTICE\nEx. 5.1 Q1\, Q3 (all parts)\, Q6 and Q12. Show
  both one-sided limits at each joining point.\n\n3. CHECK & FINISH\nFour q
 uestion attempts\, corrections and a 3-line continuity test.\n\nVIDEO USE\
 nThe linked window is a suggested continuation\, not a verified timestamp 
 for today’s topic. Check its heading first. Use it only if it explains t
 he NCERT topic named above\; if it does not\, use the named NCERT passage 
 and worked example instead. Spend at most 2 minutes locating a matching ex
 planation. Watching the whole window is optional\; stop at the end of the 
 learning budget and begin the questions.\n\nRESOURCES\nPDF page numbers co
 unt from the first file page.\nMain lesson · 0:00:00–0:30:00\nhttps://w
 ww.youtube.com/watch?v=paNnEHzOfJw&t=0s\n\nNCERT · today’s section / qu
 estions\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/lemh105.pdf#page=13\n\nNCERT av
 ailable final answers\nSaved file: Sources/Books/maths-part-1/lemh1an.pdf\
 n\n\nIF UNFINISHED\nReserve the checking time. Record the exact question o
 r step and flag Needs repair in the HTML planner. Use the 11:45 PM buffer 
 if needed\; stop at midnight. Remaining work carries into the next same-su
 bject block\, using explanation/replay time first.\n\nSAVED FILES & PROGRE
 SS\nOpen planner.html from the project folder for saved PDFs\, reference c
 ards and progress tracking. Saved files are not uploaded or embedded in th
 is calendar\; local file links do not reliably open from Google Calendar. 
 Public links above work independently. Calendar events do not sync complet
