SUMMARY:STUDY · Chemistry / Organic base — Organic base · structures & 
 bonds
DESCRIPTION:CBSE XII · Phase 1 · Day 1/9 · 2026-10-23\n1:00 PM–2:00 PM
  · 60 minutes · Asia/Kolkata (IST)\n\nTIME BUDGET\n5 min — Recall yest
 erday’s base\n30 min — Lesson and matching NCERT passage\n20 min — A
 ttempt the named examples / check items\n5 min — Check and record one co
 rrection\n\nWORK ORDER\nOpen the NCERT section named in step 1. Use a matc
 hing video explanation OR the worked example within the learning budget\; 
 do not try to finish both. Attempt the step 2 questions in the listed orde
 r with solutions covered. Reserve the checking minutes. At the practice cu
 toff\, flag any unattempted or unresolved question by number\; it goes to 
 the buffer or next same-subject slot.\n\n1. LEARN / RECALL\nNCERT XI selec
 ted 8.2–8.4\, PDF pp. 2–6: valency\, expanded/condensed structures\, s
 igma/pi bonds\, sp3/sp2/sp and functional-group recognition.\n\n2. INDEPEN
 DENT PRACTICE\nBridge check Q3\, Q5 and Q6. Sketch ethanol\, ethanal\, eth
 ene and ethyne with sensible valencies.\n\n3. CHECK & FINISH\nIdentify the
  groups and count bonds without notes\; do not memorise a full reaction li
 st.\n\nVIDEO USE\nThe linked window is a suggested continuation\, not a ve
 rified timestamp for today’s topic. Check its heading first. Use it only
  if it explains the NCERT topic named above\; if it does not\, use the nam
 ed NCERT passage and worked example instead. Spend at most 2 minutes locat
 ing a matching explanation. Watching the whole window is optional\; stop a
 t the end of the learning budget and begin the questions.\n\nRESOURCES\nPD
 F page numbers count from the first file page.\nMain lesson · 0:00:00–0
 :30:00\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZKIXgQOIZvc&t=0s\n\nNCERT · today
 ’s section / questions\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/kech202.pdf#pa
 ge=2\n\nOrganic check · questions and answers\nSaved file: Resources/phas
 e-01/organic-bridge-check.html\nThe assigned bridge questions and answer c
 hecks are included below.\n\nNCERT practice / worked model · PDF page 3\n
 https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/kech202.pdf#page=3\n\nNCERT practice / w
 orked model · PDF page 4\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/kech202.pdf#p
 age=4\n\nNCERT practice / worked model · PDF page 5\nhttps://ncert.nic.in
 /textbook/pdf/kech202.pdf#page=5\n\n\nORGANIC BRIDGE — original prerequi
 site questions\, not CBSE PYQs\nQ3. Identify the functional group in each:
  CH3CHO\, CH3COCH3\, CH3COOH\, CH3NH2\, CH3OCH3.\nQ5. State the hybridisat
 ion of each carbon atom in CH3CHO.\nQ6. Count sigma and pi bonds in ethene
  and ethyne.\n\nANSWER CHECK — read only after attempting the questions\
 nQ3. Aldehyde\; ketone\; carboxylic acid\; amine\; ether\, respectively.\n
 Q5. The methyl carbon is sp3\; the carbonyl carbon is sp2.\nQ6. Ethene: 5 
 sigma and 1 pi. Ethyne: 3 sigma and 2 pi.\n\nIF UNFINISHED\nReserve the ch
 ecking time. Record the exact question or step and flag Needs repair in th
 e HTML planner. Use the 11:45 PM buffer if needed\; stop at midnight. Rema
 ining work carries into the next same-subject block\, using explanation/re
 play time first.\n\nSAVED FILES & PROGRESS\nOpen planner.html from the pro
 ject folder for saved PDFs\, reference cards and progress tracking. Saved 
