SUMMARY:REVISION — Relations/functions\; field & potential
DESCRIPTION:CBSE XII · Phase 1 · Day 1/9 · 2026-10-23\n10:45 PM–11:45 
 PM · 60 minutes · Asia/Kolkata (IST)\n\nTIME BUDGET\n15 min — Earlier 
 maths recall / questions\n15 min — Earlier physics recall / questions\n2
 5 min — The named spaced returns\n5 min — Correct and log\n\n1. LEARN 
 / RECALL\nUse the first 15 minutes for the earlier maths questions\, then 
 15 minutes for the earlier physics questions. Use 25 minutes for the named
  spaced returns in the order listed. Keep the final 5 minutes for checking
  and logging. Recall without notes first\; open the linked cards only to c
 heck.\n\n2. INDEPENDENT PRACTICE\nMaths 65/1/1 Q32(b)\, PDF p. 17\; Physic
 s 55/1/1 Q1 and Q2\, PDF p. 5. Recall today’s continuity criterion\, fun
 ctional groups and four concentration units without notes.\n\n3. CHECK & F
 INISH\nCorrect the attempts\; append at most three useful corrections to t
 he linked chapter notes.\n\nRESOURCES\nPDF page numbers count from the fir
 st file page.\nEarlier maths · paper PDF page 17\nSaved file: Sources/PYQ
 /Mathematics/2026/Main/2413-1_65-1-1_Mathematics.pdf · PDF page 17\nOrigi
 nal paper: 2413-1_65-1-1_Mathematics.pdf · PDF page 17\nOfficial download
  (ZIP\; extract and open the filename above):\nhttps://www.cbse.gov.in/cbs
 enew/question-paper/2026/XII/Mathematics.zip\n\nEarlier physics · paper P
 DF page 5\nSaved file: Sources/PYQ/Physics/2026/Main/2383-1_55-1-1_Physics
 .pdf · PDF page 5\nOriginal paper: 2383-1_55-1-1_Physics.pdf · PDF page 
 5\nOfficial download (ZIP\; extract and open the filename above):\nhttps:/
 /www.cbse.gov.in/cbsenew/question-paper/2026/XII/Physics.zip\n\nNew maths 
 · NCERT\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/lemh105.pdf\n\nSolutions · NC
 ERT\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/lech101.pdf\n\nOrganic bridge check
 \nSaved file: Resources/phase-01/organic-bridge-check.html\nThe assigned b
 ridge questions and answer checks are included below.\n\nRECALL PROMPTS 
 — try before opening the reference cards\nRelations & Functions: State t
 he three equivalence conditions\, then outline a one–one/onto proof.\nEl
 ectric Charges & Fields: State Gauss’s law and distinguish line\, plane-
 sheet and shell fields.\nPotential & Capacitance: Explain connected versus
  disconnected capacitor changes before writing a formula.\nContinuity & Di
 fferentiability: Write the continuity test\, chain rule and correct parame
 tric second derivative.\nOrganic foundation: Identify the attacking specie
 s\, electron-deficient atom and direction of the electron-pair arrow.\nSol
 utions: Recall concentration denominators\, Henry/Raoult and which way ass
 ociation changes i.\n\nReference cards: Notes/REVISION_NOTES.md or Revisio
 n notes in planner.html.\nLog at most three useful corrections in the HTML
  planner. Export progress for AI updates.\n\nIF UNFINISHED\nReserve the ch
 ecking time. Record the exact question or step and flag Needs repair in th
 e HTML planner. Use the 11:45 PM buffer if needed\; stop at midnight. Rema
 ining work carries into the next same-subject block\, using explanation/re
 play time first.\n\nSAVED FILES & PROGRESS\nOpen planner.html from the pro
