SUMMARY:STUDY · Chemistry / Organic base — Organic base · breaking a bo
 nd
DESCRIPTION:CBSE XII · Phase 1 · Day 4/9 · 2026-10-26\n1:00 PM–2:00 PM
  · 60 minutes · Asia/Kolkata (IST)\n\nTIME BUDGET\n5 min — Recall yest
 erday’s base\n30 min — Lesson and matching NCERT passage\n20 min — A
 ttempt the named examples / check items\n5 min — Check and record one co
 rrection\n\nWORK ORDER\nOpen the NCERT section named in step 1. Use a matc
 hing video explanation OR the worked example within the learning budget\; 
 do not try to finish both. Attempt the step 2 questions in the listed orde
 r with solutions covered. Reserve the checking minutes. At the practice cu
 toff\, flag any unattempted or unresolved question by number\; it goes to 
 the buffer or next same-subject slot.\n\n1. LEARN / RECALL\nNCERT XI 8.7.1
 \, PDF pp. 16–17. Track the bonding electrons in heterolytic versus homo
 lytic cleavage\; recognise carbocations\, carbanions and radicals.\n\n2. I
 NDEPENDENT PRACTICE\nWorked Problem 8.11 on PDF p. 18\; bridge check Q10 a
 nd Q11. Treat the methyl-carbocation example as formal electron bookkeepin
 g only.\n\n3. CHECK & FINISH\nCorrect electron allocation\, ion/radical sy
 mbols and arrow directions.\n\nVIDEO USE\nThe linked window is a suggested
  continuation\, not a verified timestamp for today’s topic. Check its he
 ading first. Use it only if it explains the NCERT topic named above\; if i
 t does not\, use the named NCERT passage and worked example instead. Spend
  at most 2 minutes locating a matching explanation. Watching the whole win
 dow is optional\; stop at the end of the learning budget and begin the que
 stions.\n\nRESOURCES\nPDF page numbers count from the first file page.\nMa
 in lesson · 1:30:00–2:00:00\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZKIXgQOIZv
 c&t=5400s\n\nNCERT · today’s section / questions\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/
 textbook/pdf/kech202.pdf#page=16\n\nOrganic check · questions and answers
 \nSaved file: Resources/phase-01/organic-bridge-check.html\nThe assigned b
 ridge questions and answer checks are included below.\n\nNCERT practice / 
 worked model · PDF page 17\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/kech202.pdf
 #page=17\n\nNCERT practice / worked model · PDF page 18\nhttps://ncert.ni
 c.in/textbook/pdf/kech202.pdf#page=18\n\n\nORGANIC BRIDGE — original pre
 requisite questions\, not CBSE PYQs\nQ10. Show the formal heterolytic clea
 vage of the C–Br bond in CH3Br\, assigning the electron pair to Br. This
  is an electron-bookkeeping exercise\, not a claim that a free methyl carb
 ocation forms in an actual substitution.\nQ11. Show homolytic cleavage of 
 Cl–Cl. How is the electron allocation different from Q10?\n\nANSWER CHEC
 K — read only after attempting the questions\nQ10. CH3Br → CH3+ + Br
 −\, with both bonding electrons allocated to Br. Use a full curved arrow
  from the bond to Br.\nQ11. Cl–Cl → Cl· + ·Cl. Each atom receives on
 e bonding electron\; show fishhook arrows if drawing the movement.\n\nIF U
 NFINISHED\nReserve the checking time. Record the exact question or step an
 d flag Needs repair in the HTML planner. Use the 11:45 PM buffer if needed
 \; stop at midnight. Remaining work carries into the next same-subject blo
 ck\, using explanation/replay time first.\n\nSAVED FILES & PROGRESS\nOpen 
 planner.html from the project folder for saved PDFs\, reference cards and 
 progress tracking. Saved files are not uploaded or embedded in this calend
 ar\; local file links do not reliably open from Google Calendar. Public li
 nks above work independently. Calendar events do not sync completion back 
 to the HTML planner.
