 in/cbsenew/question-paper/2026/XII/Mathematics.zip\n\nEarlier maths · pap
 er PDF page 19\nSaved file: Sources/PYQ/Mathematics/2026/Main/2413-1_65-1-
 1_Mathematics.pdf · PDF page 19\nOriginal paper: 2413-1_65-1-1_Mathematic
 s.pdf · PDF page 19\nOfficial download (ZIP\; extract and open the filena
 me above):\nhttps://www.cbse.gov.in/cbsenew/question-paper/2026/XII/Mathem
 atics.zip\n\nEarlier physics · paper PDF page 15\nSaved file: Sources/PYQ
 /Physics/2026/Main/2383-1_55-1-1_Physics.pdf · PDF page 15\nOriginal pape
 r: 2383-1_55-1-1_Physics.pdf · PDF page 15\nOfficial download (ZIP\; extr
 act and open the filename above):\nhttps://www.cbse.gov.in/cbsenew/questio
 n-paper/2026/XII/Physics.zip\n\nNew maths · NCERT\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/t
 extbook/pdf/lemh105.pdf\n\nSolutions · NCERT\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbo
 ok/pdf/lech101.pdf\n\nOrganic bridge check\nSaved file: Resources/phase-01
 /organic-bridge-check.html\nThe assigned bridge questions and answer check
 s are included below.\n\nRECALL PROMPTS — try before opening the referen
 ce cards\nDeterminants: Write the inverse criterion and explain how cofact
 ors form the adjoint.\nPotential & Capacitance: Explain connected versus d
 isconnected capacitor changes before writing a formula.\nContinuity & Diff
 erentiability: Write the continuity test\, chain rule and correct parametr
 ic second derivative.\nOrganic foundation: Identify the attacking species\
 , electron-deficient atom and direction of the electron-pair arrow.\nSolut
 ions: Recall concentration denominators\, Henry/Raoult and which way assoc
 iation changes i.\n\nReference cards: Notes/REVISION_NOTES.md or Revision 
 notes in planner.html.\nLog at most three useful corrections in the HTML p
 lanner. Export progress for AI updates.\n\nORGANIC BRIDGE — original pre
 requisite questions\, not CBSE PYQs\nQ6. Count sigma and pi bonds in ethen
 e and ethyne.\n\nANSWER CHECK — read only after attempting the questions
 \nQ6. Ethene: 5 sigma and 1 pi. Ethyne: 3 sigma and 2 pi.\n\nIF UNFINISHED
