DESCRIPTION:CBSE XII · Phase 1 · Day 5/9 · 2026-10-27\n10:45 PM–11:45 
 PM · 60 minutes · Asia/Kolkata (IST)\n\nTIME BUDGET\n15 min — Earlier 
 maths recall / questions\n15 min — Earlier physics recall / questions\n2
 5 min — The named spaced returns\n5 min — Correct and log\n\n1. LEARN 
 / RECALL\nUse the first 15 minutes for the earlier maths questions\, then 
 15 minutes for the earlier physics questions. Use 25 minutes for the named
  spaced returns in the order listed. Keep the final 5 minutes for checking
  and logging. Recall without notes first\; open the linked cards only to c
 heck.\n\n2. INDEPENDENT PRACTICE\nMaths Q32(b)\, PDF p. 17\, again without
  the old solution\; Physics Q1 and Q2\, PDF p. 5. Return +1 day: maths Ex.
  5.3 Q1\, organic check Q10\, and the charging/discharging terminal-voltag
 e signs.\n\n3. CHECK & FINISH\nCorrect the attempts\; append at most three
  useful corrections to the linked chapter notes.\n\nRESOURCES\nPDF page nu
 mbers count from the first file page.\nEarlier maths · paper PDF page 17\
 nSaved file: Sources/PYQ/Mathematics/2026/Main/2413-1_65-1-1_Mathematics.p
 df · PDF page 17\nOriginal paper: 2413-1_65-1-1_Mathematics.pdf · PDF pa
 ge 17\nOfficial download (ZIP\; extract and open the filename above):\nhtt
 ps://www.cbse.gov.in/cbsenew/question-paper/2026/XII/Mathematics.zip\n\nEa
 rlier physics · paper PDF page 5\nSaved file: Sources/PYQ/Physics/2026/Ma
 in/2383-1_55-1-1_Physics.pdf · PDF page 5\nOriginal paper: 2383-1_55-1-1_
 Physics.pdf · PDF page 5\nOfficial download (ZIP\; extract and open the f
 ilename above):\nhttps://www.cbse.gov.in/cbsenew/question-paper/2026/XII/P
 hysics.zip\n\nNew maths · NCERT\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/lemh10
 5.pdf\n\nSolutions · NCERT\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/lech101.pdf
 \n\nOrganic bridge check\nSaved file: Resources/phase-01/organic-bridge-ch
 eck.html\nThe assigned bridge questions and answer checks are included bel
 ow.\n\nRECALL PROMPTS — try before opening the reference cards\nRelation
 s & Functions: State the three equivalence conditions\, then outline a one
 –one/onto proof.\nElectric Charges & Fields: State Gauss’s law and dis
 tinguish line\, plane-sheet and shell fields.\nContinuity & Differentiabil
 ity: Write the continuity test\, chain rule and correct parametric second 
 derivative.\nOrganic foundation: Identify the attacking species\, electron
 -deficient atom and direction of the electron-pair arrow.\nCurrent Electri
 city: Derive I=neAvd\, explain a terminal-voltage sign and state the bridg
 e condition.\n\nReference cards: Notes/REVISION_NOTES.md or Revision notes
  in planner.html.\nLog at most three useful corrections in the HTML planne
 r. Export progress for AI updates.\n\nORGANIC BRIDGE — original prerequi
 site questions\, not CBSE PYQs\nQ10. Show the formal heterolytic cleavage 
 of the C–Br bond in CH3Br\, assigning the electron pair to Br. This is a
 n electron-bookkeeping exercise\, not a claim that a free methyl carbocati
 on forms in an actual substitution.\n\nANSWER CHECK — read only after at
 tempting the questions\nQ10. CH3Br → CH3+ + Br−\, with both bonding el
 ectrons allocated to Br. Use a full curved arrow from the bond to Br.\n\nI
 F UNFINISHED\nReserve the checking time. Record the exact question or step
