  alkyl carbocations.\nQ15. Which is the stronger acid\, CH3COOH or ClCH2CO
 OH? Give the electronic reason.\n\nANSWER CHECK — read only after attemp
 ting the questions\nQ13. CH3+ < CH3CH2+ < (CH3)2CH+ < (CH3)3C+. Alkyl grou
 ps stabilise positive charge through electron donation and hyperconjugatio
 n. Resonance-stabilised ions require a separate comparison.\nQ15. ClCH2COO
