SUMMARY:STUDY · Chemistry / Organic base — Organic base · read a reacti
 on
DESCRIPTION:CBSE XII · Phase 1 · Day 8/9 · 2026-10-30\n1:00 PM–2:00 PM
  · 60 minutes · Asia/Kolkata (IST)\n\nTIME BUDGET\n5 min — Recall yest
 erday’s base\n30 min — Lesson and matching NCERT passage\n20 min — A
 ttempt the named examples / check items\n5 min — Check and record one co
 rrection\n\nWORK ORDER\nOpen the NCERT section named in step 1. Use a matc
 hing video explanation OR the worked example within the learning budget\; 
 do not try to finish both. Attempt the step 2 questions in the listed orde
 r with solutions covered. Reserve the checking minutes. At the practice cu
 toff\, flag any unattempted or unresolved question by number\; it goes to 
 the buffer or next same-subject slot.\n\n1. LEARN / RECALL\nNCERT XI 8.7.1
 0 on PDF p. 23. Recognise substitution\, elimination\, addition and oxidat
 ion/reduction\; use the conditions written above the arrow.\n\n2. INDEPEND
 ENT PRACTICE\nBridge check Q18\, Q19 and Q20. Reattempt Q10 and Q12 for co
 rrect electron movement.\n\n3. CHECK & FINISH\nName the reaction family an
 d explain the arrow movement\; leave full SN1/SN2 teaching for Haloalkanes
 .\n\nVIDEO USE\nThe linked window is a suggested continuation\, not a veri
 fied timestamp for today’s topic. Check its heading first. Use it only i
 f it explains the NCERT topic named above\; if it does not\, use the named
  NCERT passage and worked example instead. Spend at most 2 minutes locatin
 g a matching explanation. Watching the whole window is optional\; stop at 
 the end of the learning budget and begin the questions.\n\nRESOURCES\nPDF 
 page numbers count from the first file page.\nMain lesson · 3:30:00–4:0
 0:00\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZKIXgQOIZvc&t=12600s\n\nNCERT · tod
 ay’s section / questions\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/kech202.pdf#
 page=23\n\nOrganic check · questions and answers\nSaved file: Resources/p
 hase-01/organic-bridge-check.html\nThe assigned bridge questions and answe
 r checks are included below.\n\n\nORGANIC BRIDGE — original prerequisite
  questions\, not CBSE PYQs\nQ18. Classify each reaction as substitution\, 
 elimination\, addition or oxidation: (a) CH3Br + OH− → CH3OH + Br−\;
  (b) ethanol → ethene + water on acid-catalysed heating\; (c) ethene + H
 Br → bromoethane\; (d) ethanol → ethanal using an oxidising agent.\nQ1
 9. If one substituent is at carbon 1 of benzene\, which positions are orth
 o\, meta and para to it?\nQ20. For the electron-pair movement in CH3Br + O
 H− → CH3OH + Br−\, draw an arrow from an oxygen lone pair to carbon 
 and another from the C–Br bond to bromine. Explain what each arrow means
 . Full SN1/SN2 kinetics and stereochemistry belong to the next chapter.\nQ
 10. Show the formal heterolytic cleavage of the C–Br bond in CH3Br\, ass
 igning the electron pair to Br. This is an electron-bookkeeping exercise\,
  not a claim that a free methyl carbocation forms in an actual substitutio
 n.\nQ12. In the protonation of NH3 by H+\, from where to where should the 
 curved electron-pair arrow point?\n\nANSWER CHECK — read only after atte
 mpting the questions\nQ18. (a) Substitution\; (b) elimination\; (c) additi
 on\; (d) oxidation.\nQ19. Ortho: 2 and 6. Meta: 3 and 5. Para: 4. Recognit
 ion only\; chapter-specific directing rules come later.\nQ20. The first ar
 row shows oxygen donating an electron pair to form a C–O bond. The secon
 d shows the C–Br electron pair going to Br\, producing Br−. Carbon mus
 t not be drawn with five completed covalent bonds in the product.\nQ10. CH
 3Br → CH3+ + Br−\, with both bonding electrons allocated to Br. Use a 
 full curved arrow from the bond to Br.\nQ12. From the nitrogen lone pair t
 o H+. Arrows show electron movement\, not the direction in which a positiv
 e ion travels.\n\nIF UNFINISHED\nReserve the checking time. Record the exa
 ct question or step and flag Needs repair in the HTML planner. Use the 11:
 45 PM buffer if needed\; stop at midnight. Remaining work carries into the
  next same-subject block\, using explanation/replay time first.\n\nSAVED F
 ILES & PROGRESS\nOpen planner.html from the project folder for saved PDFs\
